WEBVTT

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.730
Damn!

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.960
What's going on?

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.430
There's no entrance!

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.670
Are you sure this is the place?

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.170
Yeah, but I can't get in contact with Yusei.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.150
Did something happened to him?

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.790
When the program finishes installing...

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:13.100
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:18.630
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.110
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:28.940
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:33.920
There's no need to fear

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:41.590
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:47.600
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.370
Streak to the infinite future

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:58.770
Dreams surpass their limits

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:06.880
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:39.160
Yusei Fudo  Probability of Losing 100%!

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.140
Its lock deck is powerful.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:50.380
Lock Dragon and the Continuous Spell Level 
Limit - Area B are on the robot's field.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:56.850
Therefore, Yusei Fudo isn't allowed to 
Special Summon or attack with high-Level monsters.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.350
I have to escape from this situation fast.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:04.850
This battle depends on this 
card's activation timing.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:08.230
I set one card and end my turn.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:09.980
My turn.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.940
I activate the Continuous Spell Summon Pass.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:23.420
When a player summons a monster, the opponent 
draws a card, and the player guesses its card type.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.810
If the guess is incorrect, the 
summoned monster is destroyed.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:36.130
Yusei Fudo's monster summoning probability 
decreases an additional 15%.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:41.570
Oh no!  There's now a 
limit on Normal Summoning!

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:45.010
I set one card and end my turn.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:50.830
It has five cards in its 
Spell and Trap Card Zone.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.730
It plans to lock me down, gain 
counters on Counter Force

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:58.350
and then use Counter Force's effect to win.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.590
That means I need to win before 
it has enough counters!

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.320
My turn!

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.920
I switch Level Eater from defense 
position to attack position!

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.830
Then I activate the spell card 
Synchro Gift from my hand!

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:17.230
By dropping my Synchro Monster's 
attack points to 0 this turn,

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:21.010
it gives another monster its attack points!

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:25.730
I give Junk Warrior's 
strength to Level Eater!

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.460
I see!

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:32.220
Since Level Eater is Level 1, it's 
not affected by Level Limit - Area B.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:35.270
It'll destroy Lock Dragon because 
it only has 2000 defense points!

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:38.390
Level Eater attacks Lock Dragon!

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.630
I activate a Counter Trap.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.890
Negate Attack.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:43.890
What?

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:48.710
This card negates your attack 
and ends the Battle Phase.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:55.570
Due to Negate Attack's activation, 
Counter Force's effect activates.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:00.230
When a Counter Trap activates, 
this card gains one counter.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.570
Like I thought, it negated 
me using a Counter Trap.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.480
The one last thing that 
worries me is that set card.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:15.050
Synchro Gift's effect ends, so my monsters' 
attack points return to their original points!

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:23.900
Oh no!  Not only did it dodge his powerful 
attack, it forcibly ended this turn's attacks!

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:28.650
All he did was let the 
opponent gain counters!

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:34.250
We can get in from here.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:39.510
My turn.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.660
I set one card and end my turn.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.940
It gained more set cards.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:51.560
I only have one chance to activate this card.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:55.220
I can't let its activation be negated.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:58.960
I have to get rid of its set cards.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.900
Yusei Fudo is struggling.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.440
Placido.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:07.140
What do you want?

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.840
What's the meaning of this?

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.920
I'm executing a strategy that I created.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.320
Don't interfere.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:18.160
If you do whatever you want, 
you'll mess up my plan.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.180
I don't care about your plan.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.880
I'll do whatever I like.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:25.180
Wait, Placido!

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.230
Let's see.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:29.830
It's done.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.500
Wake up!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:36.470
Diablos - the Riding Roids with new powers!

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:55.170
What's Placido thinking?

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:56.940
He's being rebellious.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.140
Weren't you like that before?

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.350
That was long ago.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:11.350
Your method of using the Signers to create the 
Circuit is too slow, so Placido is tired of waiting.

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:15.790
He'll use power to make the Circuit appear.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:19.100
So that's why he has an army of Riding Roids.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:26.620
But how did Placido know that the Signers 
were developing a new D-Wheel program?

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.130
Maybe he received a divine message.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.530
What?

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.530
It's not that strange.

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:35.500
We always receive divine messages.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:42.040
We agree that our goal is to make the 
Circuit appear, but we don't agree on the method.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:46.600
Changing our individual strategies depending 
on the situation isn't efficient!

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:49.250
It's fine.  It's because he's young.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:55.950
When I think that I might turn into someone 
like you when I'm older, I don't want to grow up!

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:00.100
Pretentious brats!

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.890
What is this place?

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.040
It's like a spaceship in 
a science fiction movie.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.610
It's not an abandoned factory.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:22.260
Yeah.  I have a bad feeling about this place.

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:23.360
Let's hurry!

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:44.360
Time's up.

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:49.270
Yusei Fudo, I'm not lenient like Jose.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.980
Your friends are also here.  Good timing.

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:56.450
I can't leave this factory standing.

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:02.450
This is an emergency message.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:05.380
This factory will be 
destroyed in ten minutes.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.810
All workers must stop working 
immediately and get to safety.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:13.310
I repeat.  This factory will 
be destroyed in ten minutes...

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:14.730
Huh?

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.500
Where am I?

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:22.880
Yusei Fudo, you will perish 
along with the Signers' dragon.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:35.470
What's this announcement?

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.780
It's counting down!

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:43.870
They're going to blow me 
up!  The Vice Director!

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.430
Where am I?

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.400
What were they making here?

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.410
What an annoying announcement!

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.660
I sense things are getting worse!

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.330
Bruno!

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:01.880
Crow.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.380
What happened?

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:07.380
We followed Yeager to this factory.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:09.020
What happened to Yusei?

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:10.530
We were separated.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:13.400
Damn!  Where is he?

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:16.290
That looks like the control room.

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:19.850
If we go there, we might see 
what's going on in this building.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.330
All right, let's go!

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:24.190
It's turned on!

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:26.020
What's this?

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.740
It can't be!

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.390
The self-destruct is on!

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.110
There's no mistake!  The self-destruct is on!

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:49.280
Self-destruct?

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:50.330
Can you stop it?

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:55.160
No!  The keyboard isn't working!

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:58.240
Yusei!

00:10:58.480 --> 00:10:59.980
He's dueling.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.710
What's that robot?

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:04.130
Why is Yeager also there?

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.720
Yusei, can you hear me?

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.610
Yusei, are you okay?

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:10.870
What's going on, Yusei?

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:12.870
Jack!  Crow!  Bruno!

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:16.590
Stop wasting time!  Hurry up and leave!

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.200
This factory is going to explode soon!

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:19.790
What?

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:22.260
I knew that's what the counter was showing!

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:25.230
Hurry up and leave, Yusei!  There's no time!

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:27.440
I can't.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:31.140
The door won't open unless I defeat it.

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:33.400
What?

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:34.600
No way...

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:36.840
Then stop playing around 
and defeat it quickly!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.840
He can't!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.810
It's using a powerful lock deck!

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:44.010
There's no time left!

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.430
Forget about me!  Leave!

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:47.380
What?

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:49.200
We can't do that!

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.820
Don't worry.  I know how to win.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.110
How can you say that you're fine?

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.310
Everyone, please save me!

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:03.520
There's no time!  Go!

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:06.760
Don't forsake me!  Save me!  There are still 
lots of cup noodles that I want to eat!

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:04.940
Yusei...

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:07.640
Fine.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.110
We're leaving, Crow and Bruno!

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:13.470
I can't leave Yusei behind!  
You can leave if you want to!

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:19.200
Ouch!  Why did you do that?

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:23.260
If you're not going to leave, 
then I'll drag you out!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.350
What?

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:27.470
You're not the only one who's hurting!

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:30.060
Crow...

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.200
Jack...

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.030
I understand.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.500
Yusei, I'll be waiting for you!

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:40.500
Please save me!

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.010
Yeah.  Jack, I leave the rest to you.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:44.940
I won't forgive you if you die here!

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:46.980
Yusei, make sure you come back!

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:48.980
Right.  Go, Bruno!

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:50.950
Please wait!  Don't forsake me!

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:52.950
Please wait!

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.950
We're really going to die?

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:58.950
I never said that I'm giving up.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:05.500
You don't know Yusei.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:10.470
He told us to leave because he 
felt that he was troubling us.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:13.840
But neither we nor Yusei are giving up!

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:17.910
Even if his chances of losing are 99%...

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:21.070
He believes in the final 1% and wins!

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:22.620
That's Yusei!

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:23.810
My turn!

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.220
Jack...  Crow...

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.190
Okay.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.160
I'll believe in Yusei!

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.230
I summon Drill Synchron!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.540
Summon Pass's effect activates.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:42.380
When you summon a Level 4-or-below monster,

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:46.270
I draw one card, and you 
have to guess its card type.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:51.740
If you guess my card incorrectly, 
Drill Synchron is destroyed.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.020
I draw.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:55.210
I choose...

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.590
A trap card.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:03.290
Correct.

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:08.230
Luck is finally on your side!

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:11.400
It's using a lock deck 
filled with Counter Traps.

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:14.230
That means its deck doesn't 
have many monsters.

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:18.200
Therefore, the correct answer is a trap card.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.170
I see!  That's why you're Yusei Fudo!

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:25.180
I activate the spell card Blind Spot Strike!

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:29.360
Until this turn's End Phase, 
my monster gains attack points

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:33.150
equal to your defense position 
monster's defense points!

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:37.930
All right!  By gaining attack points, 
you can destroy the opponent's monster!

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.890
I activate the trap Magic Jammer.

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.060
What?

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:47.260
I discard one card in my hand to negate your 
spell card's activation and destroy it.

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.700
Counter Force's effect activates.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:57.240
When a Counter Trap activates, 
Counter Force gains one counter.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:15:01.810
Oh no!  It already analyzed 
this battle strategy!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:06.170
I don't want to die here!

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.790
My wife...  My son...

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:12.240
Protect me!

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.240
My turn.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:19.700
I activate the Continuous Spell 
Messenger of Peace from my hand.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:24.130
Neither player can attack with monsters 
that have 1500 or more attack points.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.140
It's strengthening its defense even more!

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:32.130
I can't increase my low-Level monsters' 
attack points and attack with them anymore.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:37.810
On my next turn, Yusei Fudo's 
probability of losing is 90%.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.780
My turn!

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:44.030
Yusei, there are only two minutes left!

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:47.020
I can't lose my cool.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:50.950
The time limit only exists 
to make me lose focus.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:54.200
As long as I don't lose my cool, 
there must be a way to win.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.070
Double Cyclone.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:02.380
It destroys a card in both players' 
Spell and Trap Card Zones.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:09.180
Right now, I have to destroy Counter Force 
because it already has three counters.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.700
That's my best strategy!

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:15.190
I activate the spell card Double Cyclone!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:21.420
This card destroys one card in each 
of our Spell and Trap Card Zones!

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:23.130
I destroy-

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:24.830
I activate a Counter Trap.

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:26.300
Solemn Judgment.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:29.320
Solemn Judgment...

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.060
With Solemn Judgment, I 
pay half my life points

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:38.760
to negate and destroy your spell or trap's 
activation or your monster summoning.

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:46.410
It's no good!  Nothing works anymore!

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:49.350
Counter Force's effect activates.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:54.990
Counter Force now has four counters.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:58.590
If it uses its effect next turn, Yusei loses.

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:01.960
My life is over.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:05.900
Yusei Fudo's probability of losing...

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:08.370
100%.

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:15.560
We'll see about that.

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:17.010
What?

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:23.690
As I expected, you just made a fatal mistake.

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:26.390
There is no mistake in my calculations.

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:29.400
That's right.  There's no 
mistake in your calculations.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:34.100
If you use Counter Force's 
effect next turn, you win.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:39.350
In order to protect Counter Force, 
you played Solemn Judgment.

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:40.860
I knew you would.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:44.890
But since you did that, you 
halved your life points!

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:47.580
That allows me to make my comeback!

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.020
Failure to comprehend.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.290
I was waiting for this one chance!

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:58.200
I release Level Eater to Advance 
Summon Earthquake Giant!

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:06.780
Due to Level Limit - Area B's 
effect, all Level 4-and-above

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:09.500
monsters on the field 
are in defense position.

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:15.390
But Earthquake Giant's effect also activates!

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:19.860
When Earthquake Giant switches from 
attack position to defense position,

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.970
the battle position of one 
of your monsters changes!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.790
Lock Dragon now has 0 attack points!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.690
And this card of hope 
will lead me to victory!

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:38.050
I flip over my trap card Panic Wave!

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:41.730
With this card, I destroy 
one card on my field.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:47.740
The effects of all faceup cards on 
the field are negated this turn!

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:53.470
Then Level 3 Drill Synchron 
tunes Level 5 Junk Warrior!

00:18:56.950 --> 00:19:00.330
The wishes come together 
to form a new shining star!

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:01.990
Become the path that lights the way!

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:03.350
Synchro Summon!

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:06.090
Soar, Stardust Dragon!

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:09.770
Stardust Dragon!

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.640
This pattern...

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:19.970
When Yusei Fudo summons Stardust Dragon, his 
probability of making a comeback is 100%.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.240
Go, Stardust Dragon!

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:24.440
Shooting Sonic!

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:33.130
I will remove the lock.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:38.000
Let's go!

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:40.290
15 seconds until the factory is destroyed.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.290
The time...  Wait up!

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:41.750
10 seconds left...

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:42.460
9...

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:44.460
8...  7...

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:47.130
6...  5...

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:49.600
4...  3...

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:52.070
2...  1...

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:53.810
0.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:19.580
Yusei...

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:21.580
Yusei...

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.010
Yusei!

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:40.830
Yusei!

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:43.130
Yusei!

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.790
I knew you'd be safe!

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.250
It's just as you said, Jack.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.860
Of course!

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:52.380
We barely made it, Yusei Fudo.

00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:55.770
I can't believe you rescued me.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:58.140
I didn't rescue you.

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:00.910
I just didn't want to owe you.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:03.970
This spot should be fine.

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:09.380
Wait!  Who did you give the program to?

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:11.580
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:16.360
Yusei, I'll tell you one thing.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:19.730
You shouldn't get involved in this situation.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:23.490
They're not an opponent you can deal with.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:26.530
I warned you!

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:34.970
No matter who tries to stop 
me, I'll fight past them.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:37.290
Yusei!

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:43.400
Along with my wonderful friends.

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:14.270
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:19.280
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:24.180
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:29.190
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:29.390 --> 00:22:34.060
The cruel god tests us

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:41.000
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:44.870
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:50.740
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:54.660
Bond is the proper word

00:22:54.660 --> 00:23:00.640
As we fight, we understand each other

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:03.610
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:05.840
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:10.520
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:10.810 --> 00:23:13.380
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:16.850
You want to party until the morning

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:20.090
At our special place
